import java.util.Arrays;
public class RemoveDuplicates 
{
 public static void main(String[] args) 
{
 int[] array = {1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 4,5,2,3};
int[] array ={1,2,2,3,4,4,5};
int[] uniqueArray = Arrays.stream(array).distinct().toArray();

 System.out.println("Array without Duplicate elements: ");
 for (int num : uniqueArray) {
 {
 System.out.println(num + " ");
 }
}
}



Arrays.stream(array)
This converts the array into an IntStream.

.distinct()
distinct() keeps only unique values.

Convert stream back to array
.toArray();

Explanation:
 Arrays.stream(array).distinct().toArray(): Convert the array to a stream,
remove duplicates using distinct(), and convert it back to an array.
 The program prints the array without duplicates.

